// A method a reactive **handle** does not have fails like a method any other type does not have:
// `E0005`, naming the type and the method, at the call.
//
// `Signal`/`Computed`/`Effect` declare their surface as context methods and register no plain
// method dispatch at all, so every plain method call on one lands on the shared "nothing
// registered" fallback — which means the fallback is not an internal condition to describe, it is
// the ordinary "no such method" answer for these types, and it reads as one.
// expect: error E0005 at 12:1
// expect: exit 1
use std.reactive.{signal}
s = signal(1)
s.nudge(2)
